.Dd October 10, 2026
.Dt BHYVECTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bhyvectl
.Nd "control utility for bhyve instances"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -vm= Ns Ar <vmname>
.Op Fl -create
.Op Fl -destroy
.Op Fl -get-stats
.Op Fl -inject-nmi
.Op Fl -force-reset
.Op Fl -force-poweroff
.Op Fl -checkpoint= Ns Ar <filename>
.Op Fl -suspend= Ns Ar <filename>
.Op Fl -rundir= Ns Ar <path>
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
command is a control utility for active
.Xr bhyve 8
virtual machine instances.
.Pp
.Em Note :
Most
.Nm
flags are intended for querying and setting the state of an active instance.
These commands are intended for development purposes, and are not documented here.
A complete list can be obtained by executing
.Nm
without any arguments.
.Pp
The user-facing options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fl d Ar argument"
.It Fl -vm= Ns Ar <vmname>
Operate on the virtual machine
.Ar <vmname> .
.It Fl -create
Create the specified VM.
.It Fl -destroy
Destroy the specified VM.
.It Fl -get-stats
Retrieve statistics for the specified VM.
.It Fl -inject-nmi
Inject a non-maskable interrupt (NMI) into the VM.
.It Fl -force-reset
Force the VM to reset.
.It Fl -force-poweroff
Force the VM to power off.
.It Fl -checkpoint= Ns Ar <filename>
Save a checkpoint of the running VM.
The guest memory is written to
.Ar <filename> ,
the device and vCPU state to
.Ar <filename> Ns Pa .kern
and a description of both to
.Ar <filename> Ns Pa .meta .
The VM is paused while the checkpoint is taken and then continues to run.
The checkpoint can be restored with the
.Fl r
option of
.Xr bhyve 8 .
.Pp
A checkpoint can only be taken if every device of the VM supports it.
This is the case for the
.Sy hostbridge ,
.Sy lpc ,
.Sy virtio-blk
and
.Sy virtio-rnd
emulations, the PS/2 keyboard and mouse and the LPC serial ports.
.It Fl -suspend= Ns Ar <filename>
Save a checkpoint as for
.Fl -checkpoint ,
then destroy the VM.
The
.Xr bhyve 8
process exits with status 5 once the checkpoint has been written.
.It Fl -rundir= Ns Ar <path>
The directory containing the control socket of the
.Xr bhyve 8
process.
The default is
.Pa /var/run/bhyve .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Destroy the VM called fbsd10:
.Pp
.Dl "bhyvectl --vm=fbsd10 --destroy"
.Pp
Suspend the VM called fbsd10 to a checkpoint and resume it later:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bhyvectl --vm=fbsd10 --suspend=/var/tmp/fbsd10.ckp
bhyve -r /var/tmp/fbsd10.ckp -c 2 -m 1G -s 0,hostbridge -s 1,lpc \e
    -s 2,virtio-blk,/my/image -l com1,stdio fbsd10
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bhyve 8
